# Data Dictionary: Cancer Data

This document describes each variable in the `cancer_data` dataset.

| Column | Description | Data Type | Unit |
|---|---|---|---|
| model_id | Unique identifier for each cancer cell model | Character | None |
| cancer | Type of cancer associated with the cell model | Character | None |
| drug | Drug administered to the cancer cell model | Character | None |
| dose_uM | Concentration of the drug administered | Numeric | µM |
| response | Measured drug response expressed as a proportion | Numeric | 0–1 |
| high_dose | Indicates whether drug concentration is greater than 5 µM | Logical | TRUE/FALSE |
| response_percent | Drug response converted into a percentage | Numeric | % |

## Notes

- `dose_uM`: Drug concentration in micromolar.
- `response`: Original normalized response value.
- `high_dose`: TRUE when dose is greater than 5 µM.
- `response_percent`: Calculated by multiplying response by 100.
